---
description: Every product page change must use the existing leave/enter motion.
alwaysApply: true
---

# Page transitions

Do not add a new fade, wash, or spinner for a route change. Hook into the motion that is already there. New product pages must join this system on the first pass — never ship a hard cut.

## Landing (`/`)

Outside `/app`. Leave with `leaveTo` / `markLeaveHome` so the mesh can fade out, then enter `/login`, `/signup`, `/onboarding`, or `/app` with the matching enter flag.

```js
// BAD — skips the landing outro
router.push("/login");

// GOOD — landing download / CTA
onNeedAuth("/login"); // or leaveTo("/login")
```

## Mesh pages (`/login`, `/signup`, `/onboarding`)

These share the liquid mesh. Use `useMeshPageMotion(currentPath)` — do not copy the animation timers or invent a second fade.

- Login ↔ signup (and other mesh ↔ mesh) must `markAuthSwap()` and swap only the card. Do not replay the full mesh intro.
- Landing → mesh uses the full mesh enter (`markAuthEnter`).
- Reduced motion skips the animation and navigates immediately.

## In-app (`/app/*`)

The app bar stays mounted. Use `useAppTransition().navigate` — never `router.push` / `window.location` between `/app` pages.

```js
// BAD — in-app hard cut
router.push(`/app/${id}`);

// GOOD
navigate(`/app/${id}`);
```

## New pages

1. If the page is under `/app`, it inherits AppTransition. Still call `navigate` for programmatic moves.
2. If the page uses the auth mesh, call `useMeshPageMotion("/your-path")` and put the card in `.auth-stage`.
3. Intercept same-origin links, set the enter flag, play leave, then navigate.
4. Honor `prefers-reduced-motion`.
